The bug was caused by the `HASH_OF_MAPS` implementation not properly releasing the inner map pointer during the `bpf_map_elem_update()` operation. This oversight occurred due to the optimization for per-cpu `extra_elems`, which bypassed the cleanup logic in `free_htab_elem()`, leading to a memory leak where the inner map was not being freed correctly.
